      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Paradise Is In Her Eyes</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;The metal sits warm in her hand when she speaks, â€œHey, Catra, love?â€&lt;br /&gt;The pet name gets the response she wants because Catraâ€™s ears immediately go soft as she turns her head and meets her eyes. â€œYes?â€&lt;br /&gt;â€œI, um,â€ sheâ€™s barely a foot away from her now, Catra turns so theyâ€™re fully face to face. Thereâ€™s such an open expression on her face it makes breathing suddenly rather hard. But she manages it, somehow. She holds out the pin saying, â€œPromise youâ€™ll wear it?"&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Chapters 6 and 7 from &lt;strong&gt;Promises, Promises&lt;/strong&gt; but told from Adoraâ€™s perspective. Can be read as a stand-alone if you want.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
